From: =?UTF-8?q?Mikkel=20Inumineq=20J=C3=B8rgensen?=
 <6770514+inumineq@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 17 Nov 2026 13:33:09 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 2/2] config: instantnoodlep: Add SLPI and SSC dependency
 fragment
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Keep PAS, PD mapper, GLINK, FastRPC and QRTR/QMI/PDR ready before the
SLPI auto-boot. Userspace consumes SSC over QRTR; the FastRPC daemon
serves sensor libraries and configuration.

Signed-off-by: Mikkel Inumineq Jørgensen <6770514+inumineq@users.noreply.github.com>
Assisted-by: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 kernel/configs/instantnoodlep-sensors.config | 17 +++++++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 17 insertions(+)
 create mode 100644 kernel/configs/instantnoodlep-sensors.config

diff --git a/kernel/configs/instantnoodlep-sensors.config b/kernel/configs/instantnoodlep-sensors.config
new file mode 100644
index 000000000..448a713ab
--- /dev/null
+++ b/kernel/configs/instantnoodlep-sensors.config
@@ -0,0 +1,17 @@
+# SPDX-License-Identifier: GPL-2.0-only
+# Merge after the arm64 defconfig and the instantnoodlep K3 configuration.
+# Built-in dependencies allow SLPI service discovery without rootfs modules.
+CONFIG_QCOM_Q6V5_PAS=y
+CONFIG_QCOM_SYSMON=y
+CONFIG_QCOM_FASTRPC=y
+CONFIG_QCOM_PD_MAPPER=y
+CONFIG_QRTR=y
+CONFIG_QRTR_SMD=y
+CONFIG_QCOM_QMI_HELPERS=y
+CONFIG_QCOM_PDR_HELPERS=y
+CONFIG_QCOM_PDR_MSG=y
+CONFIG_RPMSG_QCOM_GLINK=y
+CONFIG_RPMSG_QCOM_GLINK_SMEM=y
+CONFIG_IIO=y
+CONFIG_IIO_BUFFER=y
+CONFIG_IIO_TRIGGERED_BUFFER=y
